  "tldr": "The paper characterizes when two exact-support linear non-Gaussian feedback graphs with a fixed number of latent nodes generate exactly the same joint family of perfect-intervention response kernels. The kernel combines an exact affine and Hall--Rado realization theorem for observed mixing matrices, a finite visible-source partition theorem that eliminates arbitrary source laws, and simultaneous principal-response constraints imposed by one common mechanism. An effective sign-invariant chart compiler and a common-lift theorem expose the genuine open content. The square no-latent projection equals the published perfect-matching object after explicit atomic row-recovery constraints, a four-node all-parameter witness proves strict refinement over observational equivalence, and a bounded-Laplace characteristic-function inversion supplies an honest graph confidence superset without latent-source recovery.",
  "project_justification": {
    "gap": "Existing results separately characterize observational law-set equivalence for latent cyclic linear non-Gaussian models, graphical intervention equivalence for latent directed acyclic graphs, or full parameter recovery under sufficiently rich second-order experiments. None gives an exact all-cancellations criterion for equality of full affine response-kernel model sets when the graph is exact structural support and one coefficient matrix and source-law tuple must serve every regime.",
